{"test":"text:nat_en.txt","n_prompt":113,"pp_s":17.549,"pp_ts":6.4392,"n_gen":128,"tg_ts":2.1581,"tg_total_ts":2.1557,"gen":"The storm came in three waves. The first was a wall of water that lifted the lighthouse off its foundations and carried it out to sea. The second wave broke the light’s lens, and the third wave took the keeper’s life. When the sea finally calmed, the lighthouse was empty, the lamp still burning, and the logbook open to the page where the keeper had written, “I have seen the sea behave in ways I cannot explain.” The next morning, the coast guard found the lighthouse, but there was no sign of the keeper. The only thing left was the logbook, and in it, the"}
